# b3Ɛq UPM™ — Ideation

## Core idea

Make every b3Ɛq platform describable as a portable, machine-readable, versioned manifest. The manifest becomes a reliable contract between architecture intent, platform composition, compiler tooling, deployment automation and conformance evidence.

## Design principles

- EBMA remains normative; UPM remains declarative.
- Platform identity and manifest schema version are distinct.
- Published manifest versions are immutable.
- Every component and capability has an owner.
- Contracts and dependencies are explicit and versioned.
- Secret values never enter manifests.
- Structural validation is distinct from semantic validation.
- Evidence is referenced with provenance and integrity metadata.
- Compiler outputs are reproducible and traceable to inputs.

## Candidate future capabilities

- Human-friendly authoring and manifest editor.
- Schema-aware command-line validation.
- Semantic dependency and compatibility engine.
- Signed manifest registry.
- Manifest diff and upgrade assistant.
- UAPC compiler integration.
- EBMA conformance evidence mapping.
- Software supply-chain provenance and attestation verification.

## Open questions

- Canonical JSON schema publication and versioning process.
- Whether YAML is supported as an authoring format with canonical JSON normalization.
- Registry storage, authentication and immutable artifact retention.
- Signature format and key-management authority.
- How to represent optional capabilities and feature negotiation.
- How to encode multi-tenant and multi-region deployment topologies.
- How to model inherited environment profiles without ambiguous overrides.

## Guardrail

Do not expand UPM into project/task management. Keep the recovered charter authoritative unless a formal ADR establishes a separate product.
